## Scenarios

### jj log numeric guard

#### defaults malformed limit values

- Verify: defaults malformed limit values
   - Expected: parse_log_limit_or_default("abc", 20) equals `20`
   - Expected: parse_log_limit_or_default("12x4", 20) equals `20`
   - Expected: parse_log_limit_or_default("-5", 20) equals `20`
   - Expected: parse_log_limit_or_default("  ", 20) equals `20`
   - Expected: parse_log_limit_or_default("", 20) equals `20`
   - Expected: parse_log_limit_or_default("42", 20) equals `42`
   - Expected: parse_log_limit_or_default(" 7 ", 20) equals `7`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 12 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-APP-JJ-001
step("Verify: defaults malformed limit values")
# Runtime oracle: call the parser with malformed numeric argv values and
# assert the default is returned rather than a crash or a wrong number.
expect(parse_log_limit_or_default("abc", 20)).to_equal(20)
expect(parse_log_limit_or_default("12x4", 20)).to_equal(20)
expect(parse_log_limit_or_default("-5", 20)).to_equal(20)
expect(parse_log_limit_or_default("  ", 20)).to_equal(20)
expect(parse_log_limit_or_default("", 20)).to_equal(20)
# Well-formed digits still parse to their own value, not the default.
expect(parse_log_limit_or_default("42", 20)).to_equal(42)
expect(parse_log_limit_or_default(" 7 ", 20)).to_equal(7)
```

</details>

